{"2896760": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Azooma Escape", "steam_appid": 2896760, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your uncle is hosting a celebration tonight, and the entire village has turned up to corner you with food, ask why your grades are what they are, and pull you into conversations with no exit. You have one objective: <i>reach the door before anyone notices you are trying to leave.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/450f0e15c6a77dfa62af8a3c1113179b.avif?t=1781179793\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras_big/450f0e15c6a77dfa62af8a3c1113179b.webp?t=1781179793 width=1560 height=628 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Azooma Escape</strong> is a comedy stealth game where the threat is not guards with flashlights. It is relatives with plates of rice. In Arabic, an <i>azooma</i> is a gathering you are not supposed to refuse, which is a problem.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What starts as one teenager trying to survive a single day of overwhelming hospitality becomes something <i>stranger</i>. A family errand that should take ten minutes. A village secret that has been waiting centuries for someone to stumble into it. This event is going to be longer than anyone expected.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Hospitality Is the Threat</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every room is a different kind of ambush. The aunt who needs a full academic progress report delivered in real time. The uncle whose stories have no ending and no point. The cousin who insists you try just one more dessert, and then one more after that. Read their <i><strong>movement patterns, time your steps, and slip through</strong></i> the gaps before someone locks you into a forty-minute conversation about a relative you have never met.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.poster.avif?t=1781179793\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.webm?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.mp4?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Use tables, low furniture, and crowd cover to stay out of sight.</strong></i> <i><strong>Crouch, weave, and learn the rhythm of each room.</strong></i> When a particularly determined chaser closes the distance and there is nowhere left to hide, <i><strong>throw a teacup at them.</strong></i> It is more effective than it has any right to be.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/61f4c7c1339eb22e4192369b3dd9b909.poster.avif?t=1781179793\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/61f4c7c1339eb22e4192369b3dd9b909.webm?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/61f4c7c1339eb22e4192369b3dd9b909.mp4?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The Festival</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The celebration has spilled into the courtyards, the alleyways, and every room of the house. Music covers some sounds and makes others worse. Street performers turn quiet corners into impromptu stages. <i>Uncle Shaddad's Culinary Gangsters</i> have locked the village down with food, and they take their hospitality very personally.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And the family is not only the living. Somewhere in the smoke and the noise, the family djinn has joined the search party, and a djinn does not lose people in crowds. Even the supernatural is on the side of staying for one more cup of tea.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/60d0c776cac9917a4035c2678f2fe4f7.poster.avif?t=1781179793\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/60d0c776cac9917a4035c2678f2fe4f7.webm?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/60d0c776cac9917a4035c2678f2fe4f7.mp4?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Reverse-stealth gameplay built around social pressure, not combat</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A festival village with its own rhythm, routines, and traps</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Pattern-reading mechanics: learn each relative's route before they learn yours</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A full cast of hosts, aunts, performers, and the family djinn, each with their own agenda</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A black cat companion who knows the house better than the relatives do</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Drawn from Arabic family life, written for anyone who has ever hidden in a bathroom to avoid a conversation</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An <i>azooma</i> is supposed to be an honour. Tonight, it is a tactical problem.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Perfect for stealth fans, cultural comedy lovers, and anyone who’s ever hidden just to avoid a chatty relative.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/bdc398c51a2d8bae983897b07d588c47.poster.avif?t=1781179793\" width=800 height=320 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/bdc398c51a2d8bae983897b07d588c47.webm?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your uncle is hosting a celebration tonight, and the entire village has turned up to corner you with food, ask why your grades are what they are, and pull you into conversations with no exit. You have one objective: <i>reach the door before anyone notices you are trying to leave.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/450f0e15c6a77dfa62af8a3c1113179b.avif?t=1781179793\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras_big/450f0e15c6a77dfa62af8a3c1113179b.webp?t=1781179793 width=1560 height=628 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Azooma Escape</strong> is a comedy stealth game where the threat is not guards with flashlights. It is relatives with plates of rice. In Arabic, an <i>azooma</i> is a gathering you are not supposed to refuse, which is a problem.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What starts as one teenager trying to survive a single day of overwhelming hospitality becomes something <i>stranger</i>. A family errand that should take ten minutes. A village secret that has been waiting centuries for someone to stumble into it. This event is going to be longer than anyone expected.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Hospitality Is the Threat</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every room is a different kind of ambush. The aunt who needs a full academic progress report delivered in real time. The uncle whose stories have no ending and no point. The cousin who insists you try just one more dessert, and then one more after that. Read their <i><strong>movement patterns, time your steps, and slip through</strong></i> the gaps before someone locks you into a forty-minute conversation about a relative you have never met.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.poster.avif?t=1781179793\" width=780 height=438 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.webm?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/827089c520bfe9f758c14cf58089a032.mp4?t=1781179793\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Use tables, low furniture, and crowd cover to stay out of sight.</strong></i> <i><strong>Crouch, weave, and learn the rhythm of each room.</strong></i> When a particularly determined chaser closes the distance and there is nowhere left to hide, <i><strong>throw a teacup at them.</strong></i> It is more effective than it has any right to be.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2896760/extras/61f4c7c1339eb22e4192369b3dd9b909.poster.avif?t=17